## Title: Furniture Finder
## Author: @Aldimar77
## Version: 0.3.0
## AddOnVersion: 3
## APIVersion: 101051 101052
## DependsOn: LibFurnitureCatalogue
## OptionalDependsOn: LibCharacterKnowledge
## Description: Adds source, material, ownership, and recipe-knowledge info to furnishing tooltips (inventory, bank, and Housing Editor). UI-only, console-safe: no external network calls, no gameplay changes.
## SavedVariables: FurnitureFinder_SavedVars FurnitureFinderOwnershipData
## IsLibrary: false

FurnitureFinder_Ownership.lua
FurnitureFinder.lua

; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; NOTE:
;
; 0) 2026-10-20 v0.3.0: removed the "hook installed" chat line printed on
;    every login; ownership line now uses the live furnishing-vault and
;    house-storage counts from GetItemLinkStacks (API 101051 returns six
;    values) instead of a vault snapshot cached only on bank open.
;
; 1) 2026-10-01: MIGRATED off the one-off Wookiefriseur data dump onto
;    LibFurnitureCatalogue (LFC) -- his new structured, web-edited,
;    self-maintaining database library. FurnitureFinder_ExportData.lua and
;    FurnitureFinder_ExportAPI.lua (the adapted copies of his hand-sent
;    dump files) are REMOVED -- no longer in the file list above, no
;    longer needed. We now read source/material data live via
;    LibFurnitureCatalogue.API instead of a static snapshot that had to be
;    manually regenerated every time his data changed. See
;    FurnitureFinder.lua's top-of-file comment for the full rundown of
;    what changed in the Lua.
;
;    This is now a hard `## DependsOn` (not Optional) -- unlike
;    LibCharacterKnowledge (a bonus feature on top), source/material data
;    is this addon's actual purpose, so there's no useful degraded mode
;    without it.
;
;    2026-10-19: confirmed (Kevin checked the Developer Uploader Tool's
;    "Find Required Add-ons" search himself) that LibFurnitureCatalogue is
;    NOT yet published on console under anyone's account. So this is on
;    us: publish our own copy as its own separate addon first (packaged
;    separately, see LibFurnitureCatalogue.zip -- pulled fresh from
;    Wookiefriseur's repo same day, now v1.2.0/AddOnVersion 1002000, up
;    from the 1.1.0/1001000 build packaged on 2026-10-01), then come back
;    and link FurnitureFinder to it as a required add-on the same way
;    LibCharacterKnowledge was linked. Until that publish exists on
;    console, FurnitureFinder will fail to find its dependency and won't
;    load at all.
;
;    2) APIVersion 101051 101052. 2026-10-20: 101051 confirmed as the live
;    API (Update 51, live 2026-09-28; Update 52 is not due until Jan 2027).
;
; 3) Console submission goes through the official Developer Uploader Tool
;    (help.elderscrollsonline.com -> "ESO Console Add-ons - Developer
;    Uploader Tool"). Console builds are UI-only and get reviewed before
;    they appear in the in-game browse menu -- this file as written
;    already respects that (no network access exists in ESO's Lua sandbox
;    on any platform, so there's nothing to strip out).
; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
